+## Dennis build
+
+A personal fork of eperdeme's 4.0 (firmware 4.1.0), with a local Windows tool.
+Save-compatible with 4.0 in both directions for everything 4.0 knows about.
+
+| Area | What changed |
+| --- | --- |
+| Language | German species, item, type, trainer and town names (`names.cpp`, `dex_names_de.h`) |
+| Regions | a region shows up only once its sprite pack is on the card; the tool offers all nine |
+| SD card | `FORMAT` console command and a "SD löschen" button in the tool |
+| Battles | EXP for every creature that was sent out (60 EXP = 1 level, no daily cap); normal wild levels never above yours |
+| Catching | catch chance per ball in the battle bag; a red NEU tag on missing species, a small Poké Ball on registered ones; catching registers the species |
+| Items | ball-heavy drops in stacks (3–5 / 2–3 / 1–2), Full Restore instead of the four small heals, Rare Candy, Lure |
+| Money | Pokédollar per win, a shop inside the field bag (buy, and sell at half price) |
+| Box | green tick = evolution line complete, amber tick = weaker duplicate; TIDY UP sends them to the Hall of Fame |
+| Hall of Fame | every farewell and every creature let go, on the internal `ffat` partition (`hof.cpp`), backed up by the tool |
+| Display mode | "Vitrine": time paused, nothing saved, a slideshow of the Pokédex for a wall display |
+| Saving | post-battle writes are spaced out; a failed checkpoint write is retried up to three times; the save warning counts live NVS entries only |
+| Fixes | a tap could dim the panel to near black for one frame (idle-time underflow in `updateBrightness`) |
+
+New NVS keys, each one entry and each written only when it changes: `cash`, `lure`, `vitr`.
+Tests for all of it live in `tools/emu/tests` (`*dennis*`, `exp`, `catch`, `hof`, `shop`, `tidy`, `vitrine`, `dexcatch`, `dimflash`, `nvsbudget`).
+
