+// Dennis build: the warning is decided by LIVE entries, not by `available`.
+// `available` also counts entries that a newer write has superseded but that
+// NVS has not compacted yet; those are reclaimed by its own garbage collection,
+// so a few saves in a row pushed `available` under one page and lit the
+// warning on a save holding a third of the partition. What cannot be reclaimed
+// is live data: warn when it leaves less than one spare page beyond the one NVS
+// keeps for compaction.
+#define NVS_PAGE_ENTRIES 126
+static inline bool nvsLowFromStats(uint32_t used, uint32_t total) {
+  return total > 2 * NVS_PAGE_ENTRIES && used > total - 2 * NVS_PAGE_ENTRIES;
+}
